## #02 — Fixed pins and honest side effects
Add app/handoff_tools.py and app/capture-handoff.json with exact pinned paths/hashes
for handoff, Clerk, return_capture and return_inspect. Follow existing app declaration
validation and error style; reject unknown/duplicate fields, altered pins, unsafe or
relative input paths before launching. Do not add user-supplied tool overrides or
search for latest. Backend owns strict binding/custody/state checks. No duplicate
implementation of its lifecycle. Preserve backend stdout, stderr and exit 0/2.
The backend writes. Never auto-retry on timeout, crash or unknown outcome and never
report writes-none when an interrupted child may have written. Avoid an arbitrary
short outer timeout that kills a successful capture halfway; if cancellation or
failure is reported, preserve the need to inspect retained state. Do not change
backend behavior, retry policy or hashes. Keep run and unrelated commands unchanged.

## #03 — Independent meaningful checks
On disposable fixtures prove app/direct backend output and exit match for complete
capture and an identical readonly repeat; changed event/payload refuse and preserve
custody; malformed binding/changed pin/unsafe path refuse without launch. Verify
backend partial/interrupted result is forwarded without invented success or retry.
Use accepted fixture setup only; no real model, live job or network. Tests must assert
counts/state and durable bytes where relevant, not just help text. Run the new command
suite and existing app entry tests appropriate to this edit, preserving failures and
privilege skips. Do not rerun unrelated suites. Keep all test writes disposable.

